titre$VINACEOUS OR ANNULATE SPECIES OF TUBARIA, SECT. CONFRAGOSA
com$ tiré de http://www.mycologia.org/cgi/content/full/99/4/569/ adapt GF  fev 2011
http://www.mycologia.org/cgi/content/full/99/4/569


1,0 $ Basidiomes not vinaceous throughout and annulus absent; spore deposit ochraceous-buff or lighter than brown; some spores remaining collapsed when revived in 3% KOH $ Tubaria furfuracea (Pers. : Fr.) Gillet complex and others (see Horak 2005  for European treatment; see Smith, Smith, Weber 1979  for a brief North American treatment)
1,2 $ Basidiomes vinaceous throughout or membranous annulus or cortinate ring present; spore deposit brown; spores not collapsed when revived in 3% KOH.
1,0$
1,0$
1,0$
1,0$ source Web $$f"http://www.mycologia.org/cgi/content/full/99/4/569"


2,3 $ Basidiomes vinaceous, red, or maroon
2,5 $ Basidiomes reddish brown or cinnamon brown.
3,0 $ Partial veil typically forming an annulus; basidiomes maroon; known from Australasia $ Tubaria rufofulva (Cleland) D.A. Reid & E. Horak
3,4 $ Partial veil cortinate and not forming an annulus; basidiomes vinaceous or wine red; from western North America
4,0 $ Occurring in ruderal landscapes with introduced vegetation in disturbed habitats $ Tubaria vinicolor (Peck) Ammirati, Matheny, et Vellinga comb. nov.
4,0 $ Occurring in hollowed bases of Arbutus in natural habitats $ Tubaria punicea (A.H. Sm. & Hesler) Ammirati, Matheny, et P.-A. Moreau comb. nov.
5,0 $ Basidia 2-spored; from Costa Rica and Martinique (Lesser Antilles) $ Tubaria bispora Matheny, P.-A. Moreau, Neves, et Vellinga, sp. nov.
5,6 $ Basidia 4-spored; from Australia or North America and Europe.
6,0 $ Pileus flocculose; occurring in North America and Europe. $ Tubaria confragosa (Fr.) Harmaja
6,0 $ Pileus smooth; known only in Australia. $ Tubaria serrulata (Cleland) Bougher et Matheny, comb. nov.
